<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116405" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡσανεί</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς
			ἂν εἰ</span></b>  (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς κἂν εἰ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					396b1
				</span></i>
			), <i>as if, as it were,</i> with Verbs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ . . πνεῦμα ὡσανεὶ προδιαλύεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					934b6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις ἥτις ὡ. πρόσχημα . . ἦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.15.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτε βλέπειν μήτ᾽ ἀκούειν, ἀλλ᾽ ὡ.
					βλέπειν καὶ ὡ. ἀκούειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.961f
				</span></i>
			; with a part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡ. προκαλούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.46.11
				</span></i>
			; with Nouns, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡ. σάρκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					1036b10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡ. ἀμμῶδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mir.</u>
					831b30
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγεθος ὡ. βοῦς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				832b15
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
